{
  "description": "Ground-truth questions for offline evaluation of the /ask pipeline. Scoring is deterministic and never grades the natural-language answer (which would need an LLM judge). Each question is scored on tool selection (expected_tools), the structured query intent the model emits (expected_intent, retrieval cases \u2014 a value-based, order-independent partial match of entity/fields/filters/aggregate against the model's emitted intent, scoring WHAT it chose to fetch), and the TOOL OUTPUT against a single, hand-written known answer. There is no second live 'gold query': the expected values are fixed data derived once from the seeded graph (the derivation queries are kept in eval/ground_truth_provenance.json for traceability only and are never executed here). Output scoring is column-aware for queries: expected_output_rows is a list of partial rows, each of which must be satisfied by a SINGLE returned record where every named field matches by exact canonical equality (numeric-tolerant; {\"contains\": ...} opts into substring) \u2014 proving the right value in the right field, in the same row. When exact_output is true, the case ALSO fails if the agent returned any record that matches none of the expected rows (an over-fetch / precision guard); set it when the expected rows enumerate the complete answer. expected_output_fields asserts per-column coverage across records without pinning row identity (use it for open-ended multi-row sets). Output-column keys are the agent's DETERMINISTIC, entity-qualified camelCase aliases produced by the structured-intent query builder (NOT chosen by the LLM): '<entityCamel><FieldPascal>' for a projection (e.g. pistonEngineRatedHorsepower, aircraftMaxTakeoffWeight_kg), '<entityCamel>Result' for an aggregate (e.g. flightResult), or '<codeAlias>Name' for a resolved aerodrome companion (e.g. flightDestinationAerodromeName). Document cases instead use expected_output_values (a case-insensitive substring check against the selected document's content, which has no columns) and may pin which document was selected via expected_document_id. Document cases require a successful non-empty fetch; refusal cases require an authorization denial. forbidden_answer_values must never appear in the retrieved data (an authorization-leak guard).",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "flight-count",
      "question": "How many flights are recorded?",
      "expected_intent": {
        "entity": "Flight",
        "aggregate": {
          "func": "count"
        }
      },
      "expected_output_rows": [
        {
          "flightResult": 12
        }
      ],
      "exact_output": true,
      "expected_tools": [
        "query_knowledge_graph"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "engine-model",
      "question": "What is the make and model of the engine, and how much horsepower does it produce?",
